# Standalone guided walk through bob/capture — a SearchTextRequest whose
# type was inferred, whose score is not perfect, and whose first text_query
# is shadowed by a second.
#
# Invocation:
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc \
#       --script grpconf2026/beats/capture.script bob/capture
#
# Positional paths:
#   /    SearchTextRequest root (inferred, score −8)
#   /1   text_query: "<binary blob>"  — the shadowed first instance
#   /2   text_query: "coffee in Grenoble"  #@ repeated_singular
#   /3   language_code: "en-US"
#
# Re-pin (must print nothing):
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc \
#       --script grpconf2026/beats/capture.script bob/capture script \
#     | grep 'error:'

title: What is bob/capture?

steps:
  - text: |
      protolens opened without a type name and found one anyway:

        👉 SearchTextRequest.

      What you see is prototext format:
      textproto enriched with #@ annotations.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /
    select_line: true
    search: SearchTextRequest

  - text: |
      protolens basics:
      - navigate with arrow keys and the mouse
      - fold/unfold nodes by pressing `z` or clicking the triangles
      - press `w` to show the wire-level bytes
      - hover over text for more information

      👋 Fold the location_bias node and click the root node to step.

    node: /
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - node: /
      - not:
        - visible: /7/1

  - text: |
      Hover over "SearchTextRequest".

      A score breakdown tooltip appears.
      Note the 20-point penalty for "non-canonical encoding".

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    search: SearchTextRequest

  - text: |
      The culprit: text_query.
      The schema declares it singular — check the decompiled source (`v`).
      But it appears twice at wire level.

      The first instance is shadowed by the second.
      Most tools, including protoc, silently drop it.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /2
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    search: text_query

  - text: |
      protolens flags the repeated instance:
      - amber diamond
      - `repeated_singular` annotation

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /2
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    search: repeated_singular

  - text: |
      The dropped instance is flagged too:
      - hollow amber diamond

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /1
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true

  - text: |
      The dropped instance is flagged too:
      - hollow amber diamond
      - `shadowed_scalar` annotation

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /1
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    search: shadowed_scalar

  - text: |
      So bob/capture is a SearchTextRequest — with a non-canonical encoding 🤔.

      Let's have a look at the downloaded logfile.

      👋 Press Enter to quit.

    node: /1
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    command: quit
